{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Seven miles from Jerusalem the evening shadows grow [Gm]
Two friends are walking slowly with their fa[Bb]ces hanging low
A stranger joins them on [Eb]the road and asks them why they [Gm]grieve
We had hoped [Bb]he was the one, they say, now [F]what can we believe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Were not our [Eb]hearts burning within [Bb]us
While he [Gm]talked with [F]us on the [Eb]road
And [Gm]opened the [F]Scriptures to [Eb]us
Stay [Bb]with us, for it is nearly [F]evening
The day is almost o[Eb]ver
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Beginning [Eb]there with Mo[Bb]ses and the prophets one by one [Gm]
He showed them in the Scriptures all that spoke [Eb]of God's own [Bb]Son
How the Christ would have to suf[Eb]fer, then enter in his [Gm]glory
And [Eb]mile by mile the stranger walked them [F]through the ancient story
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]He took the [Gm]bread, blessed it, broke [Eb]it
Then their [Bb]eyes were ope[F/A]ned and they [Eb]recognized him
They [Gm]got up that very [F]hour and re[Eb]turned to Jerusalem
The [Bb]Lord has risen [Eb]and has ap[Bb]peared to Si[Gm]mon
He was made [Bb]known to them [Eb]in the [Bb]breaking of the bread
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
